**Convention 1.1 (conditional scope and mathematical credit).** This is a
standalone sequel to [Complete Continuation Distinguishability Gap][CG],
[Joint Record and Quantum Payload][JR], [Fixed-Channel Record and Resource
Envelope][RE] and [Interior Record and Resource Reduction][IR]. Its fixed
object is the particular complete channel of CG (CG.135)–(CG.142), not the
set of all channels having its minimax error. The exact algebraic point,
source enclosures, normalization, minimax certificate and nested
preparation/control/instrument premises retain their conditional ordinary
mathematical status. They are specified below but are not authenticated
anew. A supplied proposal or independent assessment is fallible evidence;
neither an assessment nor a source identity proves a theorem.

The additional deductions are an exact spectral lift for the **full
complex** singular-direction cone, a constructive six-atom decomposition,
its exact exposed trace face and a separating counterexample to a scalar
relaxation, an improvement of the actual finite realization bound from
thirty to twenty-four branches, and a complete classification of the
resource vectors at equality in any sharp original four-sign mean. That
equality set is a singleton except at a finite nonempty set of strong
interior strengths, where it is a nontrivial closed segment.

Current JR §§34–40 already owns the diagonal/common-attainer and original
averaged/worst-history laws used here. The dictionary is

$$
\alpha=\theta_{\rm JR},\qquad \beta=\omega_{\rm JR},\qquad
\ell=\delta_{\rm JR},\qquad k=k_{\rm JR},\qquad
p_s=1-u_{\rm JR},\qquad q_s=1-v_s^{\rm JR},
\quad u_{\rm JR}=\alpha v_s^{\rm JR}+\beta.
\tag{CA.1}
$$

In particular the matching diagonal constructions, three sharp means and
worst-history optimum are reused results. Statements in the supplied IR
snapshot attributing those laws to an additional interior result, or
comparing only with JR §§29–33, must be read with this fuller JR credit.
Here that attribution is corrected in this text alone. IR's full complex
compact reduction, binary-live freedom and perturbation results retain
their separate role. JR's all-optimizer scope for the averaged and
worst-history problem is stronger in a different direction: sign
averaging fixes a live Choi matrix, not each optimizer's complete forgotten
channel or individual failure-time law.

